---
description: How to write and run tests in the CREW app
alwaysApply: true
---

Runner: vitest via `@angular/build:unit-test`. Run with `npm test`
(one-shot: `npx ng test --watch=false`). Specs are excluded from the production build.

- Prefer pure unit tests. Pure functions (`app-data-normalizer.ts`, utils) test directly.
- For a feature store: `state = TestBed.inject(AppStateStore)`,
  `state.data.set(createEmptyAppData())`, `store = TestBed.inject(TheStore)`, then call
  store methods and assert on `state.data()`. See `crew.store.spec.ts`,
  `reference-lists.store.spec.ts`, `app-data-normalizer.spec.ts`.
- Cover first: `app-data-normalizer.ts` (additive schema / migrations — riskiest to break
  silently) and feature-store mutations. Add tests when you touch store/normalizer/util logic.
- Components using `RouterLink`/router need `provideRouter([])` in TestBed providers.
- When a test fails, check whether the test's expectation is wrong before assuming the code
  is — tests here have already documented real behavior (e.g. `mergeUniqueList` dedupes
  exact duplicates only; `mergePorts` adds a `terminals` field).
